* ED - CP/M CONTEXT TEXT EDITOR

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* ED - CP/M CONTEXT TEXT EDITOR

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:ED filespec

Edits a text file using numbered line and character commands. This is the
original context editor, not the full-screen ZDE editor.

I enters insertion mode; Ctrl-Z ends insertion. L lists lines, B returns
to the start of the buffer, E writes the edited file and exits, and Q
abandons editing after confirmation. Work on a copy until familiar with
its buffer and disk-file behavior. For normal full-screen text editing,
use SYSUTLS:ZDE.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
